, 'start': 4355868, 'end': 4356440, 'confidence': 0.90126, 'speaker': 'B'}]}, {'confidence': 0.9616542600896856, 'end': 4467980, 'speaker': 'A', 'start': 4358110, 'text': "Yeah, so the channel capacity is the maximum possible mutual information between the actions you choose and the resulting states. So the channel capacity is sort of the maximum information that you can transmit from your actuators to possible states of the world. It's a form of optionality that says I can affect this many sort of possible futures. So, yeah, it's a sort of intrinsic property of an agent. And so in a product space, this is going to be affected by a lot of different state spaces. If they're interacting, like physiological, state spaces can kill you if they get too low. So I think the interesting thing about this is that it sort of encourages you to think about cognition in this sort of interrogative way because you're essentially trying to figure out what you can do. But there are a lot of, you know, different state spaces that are hindering that information transfer from your actuators to your state spaces. So I think it's very useful because it also sort of leads to explainable AI, right? You can sort of explain your intentions in terms of concrete state spaces which which have structure and explanation, things like that. I think I got off topic from your question, but anything else on Shannon channel capacity that I should talk about?", 'words': [{'text': 'Yeah,', 'start': 4358110, 'end': 4358522, 'confidence': 0.99891, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'so', 'start': 4358576, 'end': 4359180, 'confidence': 0.96027, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'the', 'start': 4359550, 'end': 4359914, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'channel', 'start': 4359952, 'end': 4360154, 'confidence': 0.99989, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'capacity', 'start': 4360192, 'end': 4360566, 'confidence': 0.96143, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'is', 'start': 4360598, 'end': 4360746, 'confidence': 0.99722, 'speaker': 'A'},