bel': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0005450345342978835, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00028375969850458205, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00026148560573346913, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment>StandardizedTesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0002184558688895777, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.00020828624838031828, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00020816712640225887, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00019332373631186783, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Sedan'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1075390, 'end': 1103990}, 'sentences_idx_start': 120, 'sentences_idx_end': 123}, {'text': 'The Omega Y is mapping you forward in the Y space and then the PY and the PX are just evolving by one step to update after you hit the goal. So after you hit the goal, you have to update by one step. So PY and PX do that for both state spaces and then of course you can do this for all of the state spaces.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0023543457500636578, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.001457848702557385, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.001160111278295517, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0010469765402376652, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0005390396690927446, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00038328213850036263, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003274671908002347, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0003140263434033841, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002630744711495936, 'label': 'Technology&Comp