p of entering the house and getting warm. Okay, so here is another route you could take where the hiker goes to the tree to eat and then the hiker goes to the lake to drink and then goes back to the house to get warm.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7280336618423462, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Camping'}, {'relevance': 0.03788653388619423, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>Climbing'}, {'relevance': 0.014563432894647121, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}, {'relevance': 0.004098949953913689, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>DayTrips'}, {'relevance': 0.002157120266929269, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>CanoeingAndKayaking'}, {'relevance': 0.001517377095296979, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AdventureTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0007050097337923944, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>BudgetTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0005116252577863634, 'label': 'Sports>Cycling'}, {'relevance': 0.00043465138878673315, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Bed&Breakfasts'}, {'relevance': 0.00035030252183787525, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>SeniorHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1172054, 'end': 1209298}, 'sentences_idx_start': 131, 'sentences_idx_end': 134}, {'text': "And so this JS is a huge it's important to keep in mind that JS is a huge operator and we cannot explicitly form it in memory because it's unless we have a lot of memory on our computer. But having this factorization allows us to chain policies together and evolve a high dimensional state vector in these jumps.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8540250658988953, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDesignAndHTML'}, {'relevance': 0.7000125646591187, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.08229514956474304, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.06990707665681839, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Browsers'}, {'relevance': 0.0005338121554814279, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0004962835228070617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0004383022605907172, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0003747699083760381, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.00036602787440642715, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>FinancialReform'}, {'relevance': 0.00032706346246413887, 'label': 'Sports>FigureSkating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1209394, 'end': 1237754}, 'sentences_idx_start': 135, 'sentences_idx_end': 136}, {'text': "So we're jumping a state vector around in this object oriented fashion where each state vector is updated once you get to some key object of interest, such as the tree with the apple or the lake with the water. So also in this example, you can see that the agent went from the lake to the house. And technically, if z, it occupies the lowest state, z zero.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.003741417545825243, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0034072918351739645, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0033549214713275433, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0014738825848326087, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0013243871508166194, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009523876942694187, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0005869832821190357, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005791895091533661, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0005779865314252675, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0005151880905032158, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1237882, 'end': 1273770}, 'sentences_idx_start': 137, 'sentences_idx_end': 139}, {'text': "And so technically it should die at the skull and crossbones on the map, but we let it finish his journey. And we haven't talked about this sort of bi directional coupling yet, but we'll do that in the next slide to make that concrete. All right, so if we have these defective states, we can define mode parameters e plus and E minus, which are just going to be variables that condition our dynamics.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.020176149904727936, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.003215345786884427, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0015908745117485523, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0008707199594937265, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0006435426766984165, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005352761945687234, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004174546047579497, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0002994938113261014, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.000299454404739663, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports'}, {'relevance': 0.00029809909756295383, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1273920, 'end': 1307378}, 'sentences_idx_start': 140, 'sentences_idx_end': 142}, {'text': "And we can have a mode function that takes any vector r and R is any vector of blue, green and red squares in the space, and we can map it to a mode parameter. So we can define zeta to map to the good mode, the normal healthy mode, if it's not occupying any of the defective states. But if one or more defective states are occupied, then we can map it to E minus.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.007661088369786739, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0028865186031907797, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0007267087348736823, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00046767850290052593, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0003858912386931479, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.00028728542383760214, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00027508180937729776, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00019379417062737048, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0001905720855575055, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.00017037655925378203, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1307474, 'end': 1341918}, 'sentences_idx_start': 143, 'sentences_idx_end': 145}, {'text': "And so that means if we have some low level transition operator that's indexed by E, that means we can split it into a normal dynamics PE plus and a defective dynamics PE minus. And you just notice that the defective dynamics is a sort of identity operation. It just sort of arrests your dynamics in the space so you can't move around, but the normal dynamics is just normal grid world movement.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.005914970766752958, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0019879681058228016, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013382488396018744, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0011488862801343203, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00037683488335460424, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.000326261535519734, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00017888292495626956, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00014436031051445752, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.00012119040184188634, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0001162637272500433, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1342094, 'end': 1369210}, 'sentences_idx_start': 146, 'sentences_idx_end': 148}, {'text': 'Okay, what we can do is we can compute a set of individual feasibility functions for each object of interest in the map. So in the previous example, we had two trees, two lakes and a house. So we have five state time feasibility functions. And then this Ada hat is an aggregate function of all of these functions where the pi is indexing the corresponding pi for that function. Anyone can ask questions, by the way, if they have any questions.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.46025481820106506, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.004500415176153183, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.003592383349314332, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013033442664891481, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.0011836923658847809, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0009489666554145515, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0007992415921762586, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0004174639761913568, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00032757120789028704, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00030143631738610566, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1369950, 'end': 1411880}, 'sentences_idx_start': 149, 'sentences_idx_end': 153}, {'text': 'All right, so the full dynamics is going to be just defined like we defined it before, where we have these two state spaces, the base state space coupled to the internal state space through F. But then we have this zeta R here on the conditioning side. And so this is an operator that you have to achieve goals in order to keep yourself out of these sort of absorbing defective states. I showed this influence diagram before, but this influence diagram is capturing this coupling.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.007020086981356144, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00459090992808342, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0016341755399480462, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0010750259971246123, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0004721727455034852, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00042576281703077257, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.00038501134258694947, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00037016611895523965, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.000359307014150545, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ReproductiveHealth>Pregnancy'}, {'relevance': 0.00032501135137863457, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1414990, 'end': 1473400}, 'sentences_idx_start': 154, 'sentences_idx_end': 157}, {'text': 'Okay, so many of you will probably be familiar with the standard Bellman equations which are formalized this way, where you have some reward function plus some discounted expectation of your future value. And so the value function in a sort of standard Bellman equation says, how much reward am I going to get if I act here optimally over an infinite horizon? And so the reward function is often thought to be a task. It has that sort of semantics in RL land.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03323202580213547, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.018961966037750244, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.011713966727256775, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0015374955255538225, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.0013706041499972343, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0011847657151520252, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0006862881709821522, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0003928012156393379, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>AngelInvestment'}, {'relevance': 0.00038449841667898, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.00030529158539138734, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1475340, 'end': 1516630}, 'sentences_idx_start': 158, 'sentences_idx_end': 161}, {'text': "And then the optimal policy is just going to return the action that corresponds to the best action that maximizes your value, your long run sum of rewards that you're going to get. So this is a recursive equation, but my thesis is that we need to rethink the sort of model based Bellman formalizations in order to compute these nice factorizations that move us around high dimensional space like we've been talking about on the previous slides. So we're going to formalize some new Bellman equations called operator Bellman equations.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.17230455577373505, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.05440933629870415, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.004155367612838745, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0031444558408111334, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0023994618095457554, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0009438687120564282, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0008828641148284078, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.0007777887512929738, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0006091676186770201, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>MutualFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.00043771398486569524, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1519340, 'end': 1566420}, 'sentences_idx_start': 162, 'sentences_idx_end': 164}, {'text': "And these are going to be non stationary Bellman equations or they're going to be functions of time. So instead of having a value function that says what's the accumulated reward that I get? I'm going to have a cumulative feasibility function kappa. And this is going to represent what is the cumulative probability that I achieve a particular goal, where a goal, remember, is an action on a higher level space. So this has a very similar form to the infinite horizon Bellman equation that I just showed.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0020998548716306686, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0009304064442403615, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0009145074291154742, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0007192841148935258, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0005959214176982641, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0004052696458529681, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00036977039417251945, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.00032583787105977535, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.000325260276440531, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.00021088164066895843, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1567100, 'end': 1605672}, 'sentences_idx_start': 165, 'sentences_idx_end': 169}, {'text': "But you'll notice that we have this availability function here for a specific goal. So this is a single goal G that we're picking out. So say the eaten apple goal or the drink the water goal. We're just choosing one. And so F is returning the availability of G from any given state and time and action. And then, so either the agent achieves a goal now, which is what this equation is saying, or which is the plus the agent does not achieve the goal.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004143863916397095, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0010701091960072517, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0008583401213400066, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.0006224606768228114, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005516472738236189, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GreenSolutions'}, {'relevance': 0.0005096430541016161, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy'}, {'relevance': 0.0004294280370231718, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.00042920501437038183, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0003756949445232749, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00032422933145426214, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1605836, 'end': 1646236}, 'sentences_idx_start': 170, 'sentences_idx_end': 175}, {'text': "So one minus the probability of achieving the goal is the probability that you don't achieve the goal times the expectation that you achieve it in the future. So it has this similar recursive structure that the infinite horizon Bellman equation has. Okay, so then we have the policy, and this policy equation is a little different from the last one because you can imagine that you can maximize the cumulative that you achieve a goal, but you sort of do it at the last second.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.007866090163588524, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.005573459900915623, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0030660496558994055, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0018314821645617485, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0016820944147184491, 'label': 'PersonalFinance'}, {'relevance': 0.0016409100499004126, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.00045169220538809896, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0002458631352055818, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoSafetyTechnologies'}, {'relevance': 0.00018216170428786427, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessAccounting&Finance'}, {'relevance': 0.0001815113500924781, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Sedan'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1646268, 'end': 1686350}, 'sentences_idx_start': 176, 'sentences_idx_end': 178}, {'text': 'You have maximized certainty that you can get to the store right before it closes. So you know 100% that you can achieve the goal of getting an item from the store five minutes before it closes. Well, it might be if the store is open for some period of time, that essentially you might want to get it as soon as possible.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7174834609031677, 'label': 'Shopping>GroceryShopping'}, {'relevance': 0.6542590856552124, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>RetailIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.15614157915115356, 'label': 'Shopping'}, {'relevance': 0.05280345678329468, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.010687205940485, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}, {'relevance': 0.0019949697889387608, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0019052259158343077, 'label': 'Shopping>HouseholdSupplies'}, {'relevance': 0.0013688162434846163, 'label': 'Shopping>HolidayShopping'}, {'relevance': 0.001167148700915277, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0010595249477773905, 'label': 'Food&Drink>DiningOut'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1686960, 'end': 1712820}, 'sentences_idx_start': 179, 'sentences_idx_end': 181}, {'text': "So what this equation is saying is that we're going to pick the action which maximizes the cumulative, but from that set of equivalent actions that maximize the cumulative, which is a star. So we're collecting the actions that maximize the cumulative and we're going to pick the one that minimizes the time.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0012341417605057359, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0007369462982751429, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0006754311034455895, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0005300854681991041, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.00045021576806902885, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>Elections'}, {'relevance': 0.0003825943567790091, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0002912228519562632, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoParts'}, {'relevance': 0.00022873554553370923, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00022040073235984892, 'label': 'PersonalFinance'}, {'relevance': 0.0001872365246526897, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>BudgetCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1712970, 'end': 1735084}, 'sentences_idx_start': 182, 'sentences_idx_end': 183}, {'text': "So this is the sort of conditional optimization that says subject to the fact that we want to maximize the cumulative, we want to get there as fast as we can normally there's just with the infinite Horizon Belmont equation, there's the value function and the policy. Here we have a third function, which is the state time feasibility function which I've been talking about.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.10864607989788055, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.007665874902158976, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.002884555608034134, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.002376569900661707, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0021224229130893946, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0009662860538810492, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>Insurance>LifeInsurance'}, {'relevance': 0.0006782528362236917, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0005589067586697638, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005143493181094527, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports>HorseRacing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004709170898422599, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1735202, 'end': 1763750}, 'sentences_idx_start': 184, 'sentences_idx_end': 185}, {'text': "And the state time feasibility function says given that I start at X and T, what's the probability that I achieve a goal g at a particular state final state in time XF and TF? And so you can compute this via dynamic programming as you're computing these other functions. And there's a relationship between the cumulative feasibility and the state time feasibility, which is that if you can sum up the individual final states and times from your state time feasibility and that is the cumulative.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.006172969006001949, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.004106191452592611, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0018828032771125436, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008365114335902035, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0005321463104337454, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.000527795753441751, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003276876814197749, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoParts'}, {'relevance': 0.00031303870491683483, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0002852088655345142, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002840893866959959, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1764360, 'end': 1808100}, 'sentences_idx_start': 186, 'sentences_idx_end': 188}, {'text': "So the cumulative feasibility is just summing over the individual probabilities of a given state final state time. And the nice property is that when you use these operator bellman equations on hierarchical state spaces, such as the product space of the agent's core ontology, it has a nice decomposition property, which is that if you're just solving to go to a particular point in the world, then you can actually compute Ada separately from the high level space.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.005514673888683319, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0023468160070478916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0022799030411988497, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0017166580073535442, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0014364906819537282, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0010861372575163841, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.001020712312310934, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.000423516146838665, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00035167907481081784, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0002835422637872398, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1808840, 'end': 1848272}, 'sentences_idx_start': 189, 'sentences_idx_end': 190}, {'text': 'So you just solve for Ada the state time feasibility function on the low level space, but then omega can be computed independently in the high level space and they can be combined. So this decomposition property is really nice because we never want to work in a product space, especially as we learn tons of dynamics about how the world works, we need to be able to compute representations in a factorized way which is going to help us move around in reason.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6203989386558533, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.04541793838143349, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.008306102827191353, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.004009695257991552, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0016881475457921624, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00141004694160074, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004873147117905319, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003588248509913683, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.00026584879378788173, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00023621847503818572, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1848326, 'end': 1880990}, 'sentences_idx_start': 191, 'sentences_idx_end': 192}, {'text': "So this means that when we compute a bunch of individual state time feasibility functions for each goal I don't know why this little hat is here, but then if we have five of these and we have an aggregate feasibility function. Then we can use this aggregate feasibility function to move around from feature to feature in the low level world and update all of our internal and higher level states. And so this is the object from the previous slides that sort of map us around the world.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.016591303050518036, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.013715390115976334, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0012023773742839694, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0011101062409579754, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0008348181727342308, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.000800256326328963, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0006690564332529902, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006631670985370874, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006380113190971315, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0005026737344451249, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1881760, 'end': 1927610}, 'sentences_idx_start': 193, 'sentences_idx_end': 195}, {'text': "So you can also do, and I won't talk about this much, but you can also do logical tasks where instead of eating an apple, you might want to gather an apple. So if you go obtain an apple, then there could be a bit that corresponds to having an apple. And you flip that bit to one once you go to the tree and then you go gather water at the lake and you flip that bit and then you go to the key and you obtain that key.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0010428373934701085, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.00046039055450819433, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.0003285733109805733, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00029223834280855954, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.00028701877454295754, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0002553850063122809, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00021787425794173032, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.00020787199900951236, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.00020365309319458902, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0001902113581309095, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1928460, 'end': 1954912}, 'sentences_idx_start': 196, 'sentences_idx_end': 198}, {'text': 'And that might be a task where you have to obtain these three items, perhaps because you wanted to compose this task with something else. You want to bring these items to another agent or whatever. So the point is that you can use these factorizations to move around the world, especially when things in the world have a sort of limited time period in which they are available. I talked about how we can plan in these high dimensional state spaces using this factorization.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.013521356508135796, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.006668814457952976, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.004853809252381325, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}, {'relevance': 0.004100569989532232, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.003874908434227109, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0032005510292947292, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0030138457659631968, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.003000417724251747, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0025604250840842724, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0016852226108312607, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1954966, 'end': 1992860}, 'sentences_idx_start': 199, 'sentences_idx_end': 202}, {'text': "And now we get to the question, well, why should I plan to any particular high dimensional state? That's the intrinsic motivation question. Given that there's an exponential number of state vectors in a product space, why is one state vector of the world in the far off distance better than another? So that's where empowerment comes in. Empowerment is an intrinsic motivation metric which sort of represents controllability. So formally, empowerment is a function of a transition operator.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.011717098765075207, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0058309040032327175, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0037497414741665125, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0032361506018787622, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0019571464508771896, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0019180596573278308, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.0017158703412860632, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0014207155909389257, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0012492501409724355, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0011938245734199882, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1993860, 'end': 2037420}, 'sentences_idx_start': 203, 'sentences_idx_end': 208}, {'text': "It's an intrinsic measure of a transition operator and you can also condition it on the state that an agent is at. So it takes two arguments and it also has a horizon n, which we'll talk about in a second. So it's formally defined as the Shannon channel capacity between your actuators or sequences of actions that you take and the resulting states. So the channel capacity, so here open loop sequence of actions would just be go up right and up again, or up left and then down.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09214529395103455, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.05363961309194565, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>RadioControl'}, {'relevance': 0.003861317876726389, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0028709648177027702, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.0018591471016407013, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0014323832001537085, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0008669705130159855, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0007661956478841603, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0006518839509226382, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0005262392805889249, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2038160, 'end': 2078330}, 'sentences_idx_start': 209, 'sentences_idx_end': 212}, {'text': "There are a lot of possible sequences of actions. So big a here is a random variable for your sequences of actions. And so for a horizon n, you can ask how much information can we transmit from our actuators to the resulting state at time tau. So tau minus T is our horizon n, which is this parameter on the empowerment. So it's just saying what's the agent's capacity to affect the future with certainty or varying amounts of certainty?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.017135856673121452, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.009139949455857277, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.008473236113786697, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0019008758245036006, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0013011748669669032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.000738640024792403, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006896181148476899, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0003456022823229432, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0003201272920705378, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.00031305334414355457, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2080800, 'end': 2122120}, 'sentences_idx_start': 213, 'sentences_idx_end': 217}, {'text': 'And so the channel capacity is formally defined as the maximum mutual information given distribution over these action sequences and the mutual information decomposes into the entropy of the final states minus the conditional entropy of the final state random variable given that, you know, given the actions and your starting state. So this means there are two sort of extremes to empowerment.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7354305386543274, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.031442027539014816, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>PhoneServices'}, {'relevance': 0.004855246748775244, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>RadioControl'}, {'relevance': 0.004604053217917681, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0031429899390786886, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0022894726134836674, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.002272088313475251, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0013683040160685778, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0010473192669451237, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.0010094594908878207, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2122860, 'end': 2162020}, 'sentences_idx_start': 218, 'sentences_idx_end': 219}, {'text': "If PX is a deterministic operator, so anytime I'm at state X and I apply an action, I get a deterministic output x prime, then the conditional entropy, there's going to be no uncertainty over my future state. So the entropy is going to be zero. There's no uncertainty. And so that means that the conditional entropy has to cancel out. And so empowerment is really just the maximum possible entropy given this distribution.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004725183825939894, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0034832654055207968, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0017546110320836306, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0013922839425504208, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0007739942520856857, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005576092517003417, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0005068856407888234, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.00033658661413937807, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.000287391449091956, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.00028248937451280653, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2162680, 'end': 2201340}, 'sentences_idx_start': 220, 'sentences_idx_end': 224}, {'text': 'And this just reduces down to the log of the number of possible reachable states. So how much can I actually reach in the world? And so if my horizon is two, we can see that the empowerment here is just log of 13. So there are 13 states I can get to, and I have perfect control, so I can actually realize any of those 13 states if I want.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0016005825018510222, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy'}, {'relevance': 0.0011805945541709661, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0009127581724897027, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0008266044897027314, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.00039898650720715523, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0003850283974315971, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0003629166749306023, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0003280080563854426, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>MMOs'}, {'relevance': 0.0002564972674008459, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0002491612685844302, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2201500, 'end': 2227690}, 'sentences_idx_start': 225, 'sentences_idx_end': 228}, {'text': "And the other extreme is, if PX is action independent, meaning that any sort of state that I'm in, I have an action, that maybe there's the same distribution given that action, say a uniform distribution, then my conditional entropy given the actions is just going to be the entropy. And so the empowerment has to be zero because this term is going to cancel out.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004080410115420818, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.003323945449665189, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0027999617159366608, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.0023333770222961903, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.001175143988803029, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0004871356941293925, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00038063820102252066, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.00037088830140419304, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>MMOs'}, {'relevance': 0.0003181569336447865, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003132255806121975, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2229680, 'end': 2265830}, 'sentences_idx_start': 229, 'sentences_idx_end': 230}, {'text': "And so there might be a lot of states you can technically reach because I can select actions and I'm just going to go random places. So Pink is all the states I could possibly reach, but I don't have any control over which state I'm going to end up in. And so I can't influence my future in any way, even though there are a lot of possible futures. So empowerment in that extreme is zero.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.13571609556674957, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>Elections'}, {'relevance': 0.05908453091979027, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.01347446721047163, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.004660329315811396, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007635854999534786, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0004976069903932512, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0003943310002796352, 'label': 'PersonalFinance'}, {'relevance': 0.00036845155409537256, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.00028481322806328535, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialAssistance>GovernmentSupportAndWelfare'}, {'relevance': 0.0002655632852111012, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2267160, 'end': 2292880}, 'sentences_idx_start': 231, 'sentences_idx_end': 234}, {'text': "And then there's an in between zone where you take actions and there's a bias in one direction or there's different distributions for each action. And so there might be uncertainty, but you can sort of control how much information. You can sort of control what state that you want to end up at. Okay, so what I'm going to define is a function valence.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.011189943179488182, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0026207314804196358, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0013129713479429483, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0012131099356338382, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0011763563379645348, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0008644924964755774, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007275104871951044, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0005955722299404442, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005950204795226455, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0005645608762279153, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2292950, 'end': 2319480}, 'sentences_idx_start': 235, 'sentences_idx_end': 238}, {'text': "And it's important to note that there's two arguments, the states, and you can include the time too, and the conditioning side. So you have empowerment and you can define an empowerment difference. So say you start at S and T, and then you end up at a future state in time after you execute some sequence of policies. So Row here appended to the S and T is a sequence of policies, and S row and T row are the resulting states.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.00527390418574214, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0040542203933000565, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0016073404112830758, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0010967723792418838, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0008381386869587004, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0007864033104851842, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0007828305824659765, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0006736111827194691, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>Elections'}, {'relevance': 0.000621866260189563, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Law'}, {'relevance': 0.0005142971058376133, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2321660, 'end': 2363590}, 'sentences_idx_start': 239, 'sentences_idx_end': 242}, {'text': "Then you can compute an empowerment difference. And this will be our valence function. So Q here is a function that I'll talk about in just a second. But we can see that our jump operator that's moving around high dimensional space is defined as this factorization. So we don't have to represent it. Remember, that's an important part. And so we. Can sample multiple policies from this or chains of policies.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.015242177993059158, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.009679902344942093, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.006034154444932938, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.005376942455768585, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010945976246148348, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009612115100026131, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.000713390065357089, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0005857599317096174, 'lab