the empowerment after some chain of policies. Okay, so say we have a deterministic operator, and this should be P, then valence is an empowerment difference. We can have a simple sort of example here where we have two hikers that are considering two different plans.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004184959456324577, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0038257373962551355, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006394318188540637, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0005377618363127112, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004371591785456985, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.000371619185898453, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003452091186773032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0003290748572908342, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.00023284149938263, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0002171750966226682, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Sedan'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2433180, 'end': 2468070}, 'sentences_idx_start': 255, 'sentences_idx_end': 259}, {'text': "And so if this tree here is like the space of two possible chains of policies, then these hikers are just executing one sort of path through this tree. They both have the same empowerment because they're starting at the same state and they're both two away from starving. So if we just consider an empowerment at the beginning, that's log of 13, and if we chain together two policies here, we can advance our internal state space and the agent will end up down at the lake.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2536923885345459, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Camping'}, {'re