.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.015042982064187527, 'label': 'PersonalFinance'}, {'relevance': 0.007554716430604458, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.005421214271336794, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0031095303129404783, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Camping'}, {'relevance': 0.0029964777640998363, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.002691400470212102, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0016109071439132094, 'label': 'Sports>Cycling'}, {'relevance': 0.0013235436053946614, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}, {'relevance': 0.0009995216969400644, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GreenSolutions'}, {'relevance': 0.0009645899408496916, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>DayTrips'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2600550, 'end': 2644580}, 'sentences_idx_start': 273, 'sentences_idx_end': 277}, {'text': "All right, so there's also another interesting so in this past example, we're just sort of changing the structure we're just changing the initial state. But since empowerment is also a function of a transition operator, and our operator Bellman equations are producing transition operators that map us from state time to state time, then the output of those Bellman equations, the operator Bellman equations, produce transition operators so we can compute their empowerment. So that's a deep connection between Bellman equations and these intrinsic motivation metrics.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.001636379398405552, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0015193955041468143, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0009189886623062193, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006786973681300879, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005917540402151644, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.000334408658090978